<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Harisimhadeva</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">reigned c. 1304–1324</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Harisimhadeva was the last king of the Karnat dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mithila">Mithila</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bihar">Bihar</a>. He sponsored the codification of Maithil <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahmins">Brahmin</a> genealogies in the panji registers, and his minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jyotirishvara-thakur">Jyotirishvara Thakur</a> wrote the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/varna-ratnakara">Varna Ratnakara</a>. When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghiyath-al-din-tughluq">Ghiyath al-Din Tughluq</a> invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tirhut">Tirhut</a> in 1324 he fled into the hills of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a>.</p></div>
